# API / Backend

Full rules: `.ai/rules/api.md`, `.ai/rules/backend.md`, `.ai/rules/database.md`, `.ai/rules/security.md`

## Route handlers

```js
export const dynamic = "force-dynamic";
// connectDB() when using Mongoose
// getSession() for auth — return 401 when required
// Response.json(data) or { success: false, message }, status
```

- Match existing response shapes in neighboring routes
- Do not return `200` with an error body for failures
- Validate input; use `400` for bad client data, `403` for forbidden, `404` for missing

## Auth & users

- Sessions: `getSession` from `@/lib/getSession`
- Users live in Better Auth MongoDB — use `@/lib/users.js` (`findUserById`, `enrichWithUsers`, etc.)
- Do not invent a Mongoose User model or call non-existent Better Auth admin APIs

## Models

- Pin/Board/Comment user refs are **strings** (auth user ids), not ObjectId user refs
- Pin `board` stores album/board id string (or legacy title) — keep both filters when querying albums
- Prefer extending existing models over parallel schemas

## Security

- Never trust client for role/ownership — check session server-side
- No secrets in `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` beyond intended public keys
- Blocked users: follow existing `getBlockedUserIds` / session blocked patterns

